# Ported from boltkit test/scripts/v4.0/return_1_as_x.bolt
# (neo4j-drivers/boltkit, branch 4.3 at 687a479).
# Adapted to Bolt 4.4: the version is 4.4, `!: AUTO RESET` is dropped (it
# tells boltkit's stub server to answer RESET; this harness is the client),
# and the RUN SUCCESS asserts only `fields`, as `$x`: a server names an
# unaliased column by its expression text, as Neo4j does (boltkit's stub
# answered `x`, and its `"qid": 789` was an invented value).
!: BOLT 4.4
!: AUTO HELLO
!: AUTO GOODBYE

C: RUN "RETURN $x" {"x": 1} {}
   PULL {"n": -1}
S: SUCCESS {"fields": ["$x"]}
   RECORD [1]
   SUCCESS {}
